w I hope to achieve this  in the near future so this is one of the  this is the quote from the article that  kind of stood out for me  disabled Americans are about three times  as likely as those with a disability to  say they never go online 22% versus 8%  according to a Pew Research Center  survey conducted in the fall of 2016 so  that's quite a big gap  and so I'm gonna start with my story  here so I graduated from Cal State San  Marcos it's about a maybe a 25 20 25  minute drive from here actually and I  scheduled in December of 2012 and I  graduated with Visual and Performing  Arts  Technology degree so this is basically  like a graphic digital graphic design  and it took me about a year to find a  full-time job and part of this is  because like as you know when you're  trying to find your first job it can be  really really difficult just because  you're trying to stand out from other  applicants and getting your first job is  always the most difficult thing but in  my case since I was I'm raised in  Southern California I have these eye  conditions I am not legally allowed to  drive so often when I had an interview  and the employer might be asking  reasonably so of course like how would  you get to work and most of the times I  couldn't figure out like how to answer  that question and so I started looking  for places that would have a better  public transportation system something  like yeah  maybe in New York City or perhaps like  Portland Seattle just anything that  could kind of help me get to work on  Simon in during this timeframe I  actually got in contact with someone via  LinkedIn and I ended up in Tokyo Japan  we're just crying big ya jump I'm not  going to get too much into like the  cultural differences in this  presentation unfortunately but here I'm  just going to talk about like a little  bit of  like what I found when I've been living  there this is a disclaimer some of the  points or advice that I'm gonna give out  in this presentation might be